# Packaging & releases

- **Single source of truth = the git tag** (`vX.Y.Z`). The release workflow
  stamps the workspace `version`, the `la-core` dependency `version`, and
  `desktop/package.json`. If you touch versioning, update **all three** stamps
  together — a stale `la-core` dep version breaks CLI resolution.
- `tauri.conf.json` has **no** `version` field; it inherits the workspace crate
  version. Bundle targets are `deb`, `rpm`, `appimage`.
- Distribution channels and their files:
  - Snap → `snap/snapcraft.yaml` (name `linux-ai`, strict confinement).
  - Flatpak → `packaging/flatpak/dev.linux_ai.app.yml` (id uses `_`, not `-`).
  - AUR → `packaging/aur/PKGBUILD` (`linux-ai-bin`, repacks the `.deb`).
  - crates.io → `.github/workflows/publish-crates.yml` (`la-core` then
    `linux-ai-cli`).
- Keep CLI artifact/name as `lai`. Keep the product name "Linux AI".
